    {
      "slug": "suet",
      "term": "Suet",
      "definition": "The hard fat from around the kidneys of beef or lamb. Shredded suet is sold in packets in supermarkets and is the traditional fat for British dumplings and steamed puddings. It melts slowly during cooking, which gives dumplings their characteristic texture."
    }
